{
  "id": "ss.relic.chrysalis",
  "name": "Chrysalis",
  "description": "A chrysalis case split down the middle and the two halves peeled back, hinged at the bottom and leaning apart by different amounts, and climbing out from between them the thing that was inside: a flame of white with gold around it, round where it still sits in the case and drawn up to a point well above it, brighter than anything else on the plate. The light is the subject — the relic is one more life, and the case is only there to have been left. Each half is dusky violet outside with its inner face turned pale toward the glow, so they read as two sides of one case and not two seeds. The first pass stood the halves upright and level with a bright almond between them, and that is an eye; this one splays them unevenly and makes the light a flame rather than an almond, standing taller than the case — a thing getting out rather than a thing looking.",
